{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: scVI n200 (config_004, acc 0.520) outperforms PCA n2000 (config_001, acc 0.485) for single-profile RNA, and image-only (config_010, acc 0.208) is very weak. All completed experiments use single-profile; the multiprofile axis is entirely untested. Question: Does moving from single-profile to multiprofile with simple avgpool aggregation improve performance when paired with the best RNA encoder (scVI n200)? This isolates the structural effect of multiprofile + aggregation as a single design decision (aggregation is a necessary consequence of multiprofile). Why this is the best next experiment: The multiprofile decision gates roughly half the remaining search space (configs 002-003, 005-006, 008-009, 011-012, 014-015, 018-027, 030-039, 042-051). If multiprofile+avgpool with scVI does not beat single-profile scVI, we can deprioritize all multiprofile variants and focus on encoder choice and fusion. If it does help, we gain a strong prior for investing in multiprofile+transformer and multimodal multiprofile configurations. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential unexplored design axis."
}

